Issue is in first bind mount container is instructed toi use host's files instead of container and node modules of host machine eg windows cant run on linux env so we create a volume which would tell the container dont use host's files for this specific directory instead use volume stored node modules if no data in volume exits container copies content from the image which was built to avoid node modules conflict
It's saying "use this separate volume for at /app/node_modules ." If that volume is initially empty, Docker may populate it from the 
existing image contents at that mount point when the container is first created. After that, the volume has its own contents.

